<p>Repayment or forgiveness status was not seen: the API fields did not show it. SBA loan data is not itself a record of default. No contracts, grants or cooperative agreements were found for either name.</p>

<p>No USAspending recipient was found for Abebe Holdings, Abebe St George, or Renewal Development Group (the search for "renewal development" returned only unrelated names).</p>

<h3>What was searched and not found</h3>

<p>SEC EDGAR full-text search (2001 onward), each phrase in quotes: "Abebe Ventures", "Abebe St George", "Abebe Holdings", "Abebe Blackbelt", "Mike Abebe", "249 Milton Ave", "249 Milton Avenue", "Renewal Development Group", "Ensley District Developers": 0 hits each. SEC company-name search for "renewal development" and "ensley district": "No matching companies". SEC litigation releases and administrative proceedings, the site's own filter: "abebe" and "renewal development": "No Results match the chosen filters".</p>

<p>Federal exclusions list (the open part of SAM.gov): searches for "abebe ventures", "abebe holdings", "abebe st george", "renewal development group" and "ensley district developers", first 50 loose matches each: no record with any of those names. Not re-run by the checker. On the mirror: no company named "St George Crossing"; no "Renewal Development Group" in Delaware; no Abebe entity with "Sylvan" in its name.</p>

<p>Not run, which is different from nothing found: any open-web sweep for crowdfunding, EB-5 or opportunity-zone listings; Georgia Securities Division orders (refused); USAspending's search form; the Delaware registry; federal contractor registrations (login).</p>

<h2>What a Party Says</h2>

<p>abebe.com/partnership says: "Abebe Ventures is dedicated to creating lasting opportunities for businesses, investors, and cities to grow and thrive together." None of the pages opened offers an investment, states terms, or names a fund. Pages opened: abebe.com home, /partnership, /partner-with-us and two project pages; sgcrossing.com home and about; one Direct Invest page; and the June 16, 2026 Renewal release. No open-web sweep was run.</p>

<h2>Open Questions</h2>

<div class="fact-grid">
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>Who are the officers or members of each entity? The mirror shows "officers available, please log in" and hides names; the registry does not list the members or managers of an LLC.</p>
</div>
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>The site's earlier list shows "Active/Owes Current Year AR" for the Georgia entities, and the mirror, as read October 7, 2026, shows "Active/Compliance" for each. Which date does each reflect? The mirror's data-freshness date needs a login.</p>
</div>
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>The site's earlier list shows Abebe Cox Ventures LLC as "Admin. Dissolved" with a different agent, and the mirror shows a reinstatement filed May 18, 2026. What do the state's filing images show, and who signed the reinstatement?</p>
</div>
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>ABEBE HOLDINGS LLC. prints Feb 2, 2006 on a filing line and Jan 18, 2006 on the officer list; 441 VENTURES LLC prints Apr 13, 2012 and Apr 20, 2012. Which is the formation date of each?</p>
</div>
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>Were the five federal small-business loans repaid or forgiven? The USAspending fields read did not show it.</p>
</div>
<div class="fact-card">
<span>Open Question</span>
<p>What is the current status of the District of Columbia and Maryland registrations? The mirror's dates for the DC entity are behind a login, and its pages' addresses were not recorded.</p>
</div>
</div>

